From 7245ba01bdc8e22ae66f61c0947138135ccdd84f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <claude@mabn.pl>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 05:48:44 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 04/15] headless demo replay: skip prev-frame transform save
 (draw interpolation state)

CUnitHandler::UpdatePreFrame + CFeatureHandler::UpdatePreFrame save, for
every active unit/feature every sim frame, the previous-frame object
transform (WorldObject::preFrameTra, a matrix->quaternion conversion per
object) and every model piece's prev model-space transform - state whose
only readers are draw-side interpolation (Rendering/: drawPos,
ModelDrawerData transform upload). Headless demo replay draws ~1 fps and
nothing reads the result, so gate both calls out under
HEADLESS && gameSetup->hostDemo, the same output-safe pattern as the
unsynced-cuts patch.

Sync-safety: the pass only wrote draw-only fields (plain, not Synced*
types - no sync-checksum contribution) and its lazy piece-transform
refresh via GetModelSpaceTransform() is idempotent - later synced readers
recompute identical values on demand. Projectiles maintain their own
preFrameTra (used by synced ground collision) in CProjectile, untouched
here.

Profiled cost of the skipped pass (unpatched 8v8 58530-frame benchmark):
Sim::Unit::UpdatePreFrame 73 s + Sim::Features::UpdatePreFrame 13 s of a
1145 s sim (~7.5%); small replay ~10% of sim.
---
 rts/Game/Game.cpp | 15 +++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rts/Game/Game.cpp b/rts/Game/Game.cpp
index 5efed3c..f2649f4 100644
--- a/rts/Game/Game.cpp
+++ b/rts/Game/Game.cpp
@@ -1749,8 +1749,23 @@ void CGame::SimFrame() {
 
 		// Lua unit scripts change piece positions and orientations in eventHandler.GameFrame(gs->frameNum);
 		// so we need to save the previous unit state before it happened
+#ifdef HEADLESS
+		// [barreplay] the prev-frame transforms saved here (WorldObject::preFrameTra,
+		// LocalModelPiece::prevModelSpaceTra) exist only for draw-time interpolation:
+		// every reader lives under Rendering/ (drawPos, model-transform upload). In a
+		// headless demo replay nothing consumes them, so skip the whole per-object
+		// per-frame save pass. The lazy piece-transform refresh this pass triggered
+		// via GetModelSpaceTransform() is idempotent and deterministic - any later
+		// synced reader (weapon aim, script GetPiecePos) recomputes identical values,
+		// and none of the skipped state feeds the sync checksum.
+		if (gameSetup == nullptr || !gameSetup->hostDemo) {
+			unitHandler.UpdatePreFrame();
+			featureHandler.UpdatePreFrame();
+		}
+#else
 		unitHandler.UpdatePreFrame();
 		featureHandler.UpdatePreFrame();
+#endif
 
 		{
 			SCOPED_TIMER("Sim::GameFrame");
-- 
